# Swaps: Baseline v0, piece by piece

There is no dataset [P15], so no row cites a D tag. The "regime" here is the threat model [P3], the ERC-7562 validation rules [E2], a 1-week build by 2-4 strong Solidity devs [P16], and assumed generalist plus protocol-literate judges [A1]. X1 (the attack-suite pass rate) is defined in Phase D and logged in EXPERIMENTS.md during the build.

| Piece | Baseline | Best alternative [E#] | Swap? | Why in this regime |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Data / eval set | none; ad hoc tests | Attack suite modelled on AgentDojo/WASP end-to-end attacker-goal scoring, with every attack mapped to an on-chain outcome (reverted, bounded loss) [E27][E28][E29] | **Swap** (build our own) | No dataset [P15][A4]. Benchmarks mock their finance tools, so "attack success" there is not "funds lost" (failure map). Our score must be counted in tx outcomes. |
| Account | SimpleAccount fork | ERC-7579 modular account (Kernel, Nexus) + session validator [E3][E6][E7] | **Keep** SimpleAccount-style account; write the policy as one separate `AgentPolicy` contract with a 7579-shaped validator/hook interface (installing it on Nexus is a stretch goal) | Owning the account lets us close the ERC-1271 path and the self-call/upgrade path (T2, T12) in code we control. Full 7579 compliance adds days that no generalist judge sees [A1]. |
| EntryPoint | unspecified | v0.8: userOpHash becomes an EIP-712 typed hash [E5] | **Swap**: pin v0.8 only | One pinned version removes the v0.7/v0.8 hash ambiguity (replay row of the failure map). Typed hashes make owner prompts readable (R11). Bundler support on Base Sepolia is an assumption to check on day 1. |
| Signature check | ecrecover over userOpHash | OZ ECDSA with malleability checks; EntryPoint 2D nonce with one key per session [E1] | **Keep** (baseline already uses this) | It is standard and correct. The work is in tests (wrong chain, wrong EntryPoint, replayed nonce), not in a new primitive. |
| Policy expression | target+selector allowlist; decoded amount for transfer/approve | Per-parameter conditions as in Zodiac Roles [E16]; composable caveats [E13]; Kernel call policy [E6] | **Partial swap**: one declarative struct. Decode the recipient and amount for the ERC-20 `transfer`/`approve`/`transferFrom` and native-value paths; any other (target, selector) pair must be explicitly allowed. | A target-only allowlist misses the ERC-20 `to` (T4). Only Zodiac decodes parameters, and it is a Safe module [E16]. A general condition language is too much to build and test in a week. |
| Spend metering | decoded amount argument | Measure the balance delta of tracked assets around the call, in execution | **Swap** (candidate differentiator, scored in WIN.md) | Decoding only covers functions we know. Any allowed merchant function (`buy()`, a router) can move tokens we never decode. A balance delta counts what actually left, whatever the calldata said. |
| Daily limit | counter in execution | Rolling window or token bucket in execution; periodic buckets reset [E14][E17]; TIMESTAMP is banned in validation [E2] | **Swap**: token bucket (refill rate = dailyCap/86400 per second), checked in execution | A calendar bucket allows 2x spend at the boundary (T7). Execution is the only phase that may read time [E2]. |
| Per-tx limit | decoded amount ≤ cap in validation | balance delta ≤ cap in execution, plus the decoded amount as an early reject in validation | **Swap** (pairs with metering) | The early reject keeps bundlers from carrying ops that are sure to fail. The delta is the real bound. |
| Expiry | `validUntil` in validationData | same [E1][E2] | **Keep** | It is already right, and ERC-7562 forces it [E2]. |
| Gas | not handled | Cap `maxFeePerGas`, gas limits and `paymasterAndData` per agent op in validation (the UserOp fields may be read there) | **Swap** (small) | With no paymaster, a leaked key can burn the prefund through fees (T5). |
| Off-UserOp signatures (ERC-1271) | not considered | Smart Sessions has ERC-1271 policies [E7]; Kernel has a signature policy [E6] | **New piece**: `isValidSignature` refuses the agent key by default; an x402 exception parses the EIP-3009 typed data and applies the same policy (candidate differentiator) | x402 "exact" = EIP-3009 `transferWithAuthorization` [E20]; USDC [E21] and Permit2 [E22] accept contract signatures, so an agent key that 1271 accepts spends with no UserOp at all. |
| Out-of-policy approval | owner signs the UserOp | Owner signs an EIP-712 approval bound to the exact callData hash, account, chain and nonce. The UI renders the decoded calldata, never the agent's text (ERC-7730-style clear signing as in allowance.eth [E40]) | **Swap** | Permit-style phishing was 38% of large 2025 losses, driven by misleading signing requests [E26]. An injected agent writes the request text, so that text is untrusted (T11). |
| Revocation | none | one owner tx flips `revoked`; validation checks it | **Keep** (simple flag) | R14 needs it; nothing more complex helps. |
| Agent | scripted bot | open-weight LLM agent (pick the backbone from b3 [E30]) plus the scripted bot for the suite | **Swap** for the demo; keep the bot for tests | "Any open model" [P10][A3]. Model-level defenses fail [E39], so the agent stays untrusted and the model choice does not affect security. |
| Agent-side defense | none | CaMeL [E24], injection detectors [E23] | **Keep none** (by design) | Adaptive attacks beat 12 defenses at >90% ASR [E39]. The wallet must hold with a fully hijacked agent [P3]. |
| Off-chain policy engine | none | CDP [E18], Privy [E19], presidio-x402 [E38] | **Keep none** | They are bypassed by a key or host leak (failure map). Stay on-chain. |
| Recipient risk | static allowlist | TRACE score as an escalate-only signal [E34] | **Stretch only** | Useful as a "send to owner" trigger, but it can never loosen an on-chain cap, and the trace-api middleware failed open before (prior_work.md). |
| Testing | Foundry unit tests | Foundry fuzz and invariant tests; DeFiHackLabs-style replays [E31]; bundler-spec-tests [E32] | **Swap**: invariant "spent in any 24 h window ≤ dailyCap" plus fuzzed calldata; run bundler compatibility once | Security correctness is the criterion protocol-literate judges probe [A1]. |
| UI | approval web page | owner dashboard: plain-words policy, approval inbox with decoded intent, one-click revoke | **Keep simple** | Generalist judges [P15]. Design polish beyond clarity earns little. |
| Deployment | Base Sepolia | Base mainnet (user already runs x402 there [A2][A5]) | **Keep** testnet; mainnet only for one x402 receipt, as a stretch | The demo needs explorer links, not real money. |
